What was used, and what was changed:

1. references/review-triage.md
   - "Review comment agreement criteria" and "CI classification checklist":
     copied verbatim from .codex/skills/babysit-pr/references/heuristics.md,
     marked "(babysit-pr, verbatim)". Unchanged.
   - The "How ci-land applies it" notes after each are new text. They narrow
     the upstream behaviour: ci-land never posts replies, never resolves
     human threads, and reruns a flaky check once per head instead of up to
     three times.

2. SKILL.md and references/gh-commands.md
   - The rule on PENDING reviews originated as a paraphrase of
     .codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md's "Only act on published feedback.
     Ignore review submissions in GitHub's `PENDING` state and inline
     comments attached to those pending reviews." SKILL.md's Phase 1 has
     since been rewritten again to state only what the pinned round query
     can determine: it returns submitted reviews only, so nothing pending
     is visible or acted on.
   - The explanation of why the job logs endpoint is preferred over
     `gh run view --log-failed` is quoted verbatim from
     .codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md, marked as such.
   - The accepted PR inputs (no argument, PR number, PR URL) are adapted from
     .codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md: the reference to the upstream watcher
     script's `--pr auto` option was removed, because ci-land ships no script.
   - The rule to resolve a review thread only after the push succeeds is
     adapted from .codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md. Changed: ci-land leaves
     no comment when resolving, and posts nothing on the pull request at all.

No upstream code (the watcher script) is included.

