What was used, and what was changed:

1. references/gh-commands.md ("Two reviewers behind the `cursor` login")
   and references/review-triage.md ("Bugbot pass keys")
   - The body tokens `cursor_automation_id` and `agentic security review`,
     and the pass-key prefixes `RUN_ID:` and `CURSOR_AUTOMATION_ID:`, are
     taken verbatim from scripts/watch-pr/github.ts, which treats every such
     `cursor` post as one Bugbot family. The surrounding rules are new text:
     ci-land splits the `cursor` login into one reviewer per check name for
     its push gate (the tokens do not tell them apart), and uses the pass key
     only as a dedupe aid, never as a reason to skip a thread.

2. references/review-triage.md (DECLINE)
   - Three DECLINE signals are restated in new words from
     references/bugbot-triage.md's candidate patterns: a security finding
     already fixed by a later commit in the same PR, a fix that would widen a
     deliberately narrow error condition, and a drift claim that running the
     contract test disproves. No sentence of the original is copied. Changed:
     upstream dismisses with a reply and resolves the thread; ci-land posts
     nothing and leaves a DECLINE thread open.

No upstream code (the watch-pr script) is included.
